WEBVTT

NOTE week05-clip1-post-training
NOTE Narration read by an AI-generated voice.
NOTE The clip has its own caption along the bottom of the frame, so these cues
NOTE are placed near the top to keep the two from overlapping.

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.094 line:2 align:center
A pretrained model only
continues the text it is given.

2
00:00:04.094 --> 00:00:08.749 line:2 align:center
We gave the base Qwen3 model the
start of a discharge summary,

3
00:00:08.749 --> 00:00:13.950 line:2 align:center
and it simply kept writing a
note about a different patient.

4
00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:16.755 line:2 align:center
Now we ask it a question about the note.

5
00:00:16.755 --> 00:00:20.077 line:2 align:center
The base model does not
answer like an assistant.

6
00:00:20.077 --> 00:00:25.750 line:2 align:center
It treats the text as a quiz and
keeps inventing new questions.

7
00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:31.463 line:2 align:center
The post-trained version of the same
model answers the question directly.

8
00:00:31.463 --> 00:00:37.401 line:2 align:center
But here its answer is wrong: the note
says the patient denies chest pain.

9
00:00:37.401 --> 00:00:41.683 line:2 align:center
Clips three and four show
two ways to fix this.

10
00:00:41.883 --> 00:00:46.701 line:2 align:center
Post-training adds stages after
pretraining: supervised fine-tuning,

11
00:00:46.701 --> 00:00:48.331 line:2 align:center
then preference tuning,

12
00:00:48.331 --> 00:00:53.008 line:2 align:center
then reinforcement learning with
rewards that a program can check.

13
00:00:53.008 --> 00:00:56.350 line:2 align:center
We cover the last stage in clip four.

14
00:00:56.550 --> 00:01:01.151 line:2 align:center
Supervised fine-tuning trains
on instruction and answer pairs.

15
00:01:01.151 --> 00:01:04.134 line:2 align:center
Each pair is wrapped in a chat template,

16
00:01:04.134 --> 00:01:07.723 line:2 align:center
with special markers for
where the user's turn

17
00:01:07.723 --> 00:01:11.350 line:2 align:center
and the assistant's turn begin and end.

18
00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:15.561 line:2 align:center
The loss is the same next-token
loss as in pretraining.

19
00:01:15.561 --> 00:01:19.268 line:2 align:center
The only difference is that it
is counted on the answer tokens,

20
00:01:19.268 --> 00:01:24.217 line:2 align:center
not on the instruction, so the
model learns to write answers.

21
00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:28.696 line:2 align:center
So the architecture is the
same and the loss is the same.

22
00:01:28.696 --> 00:01:34.846 line:2 align:center
Only the training data changes, from raw
text to instruction and answer pairs,

23
00:01:34.846 --> 00:01:39.780 line:2 align:center
and that is what turns a text
generator into an assistant.
